1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,250
As winter takes its icy grip, and we head outside into a cold and crisp morning, we might be dreaming of warmer and sunnier days that lie ahead.
当冬天寒气逼人，我们顶着凛冽清新的晨风出门时，心里或许会憧憬着即将到来的温暖艳阳天。

2
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:24,460
Although, for many, summer might give us the most clement weather, our changing climate might mean that our chilly winter season becomes a thing of the past.
对很多人来说，夏天的天气或许最为宜人，但气候变化可能会让寒冷的冬季成为历史。

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,250
So maybe we should enjoy it while we can.
所以，或许我们该趁还能享受冬日，好好珍惜它。

4
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:41,770
Last year, the World Meteorological Organization found that the Earth continued to endure a period of significant heating, making it one of the three hottest years on record.
去年，世界气象组织发现，地球仍处于显著升温阶段，去年也因此成为有记录以来最热的三个年份之一。

5
00:00:41,770 --> 00:00:51,040
The most notable warmth was in the Siberian Arctic, where temperatures were 5°C above average.
升温现象最明显的区域是西伯利亚北极地区，当地气温比平均值高出了5摄氏度。

6
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:57,310
The evidence shows that much of this climate warming is driven by human activity.
有证据表明，气候变暖在很大程度上是由人类活动导致的。

7
00:00:57,310 --> 00:01:09,820
With a shift in meteorological conditions, we’re likely to see more record-breaking temperatures, where, in certain places, summers will be scorching hot and winters mild.
随着气象条件的转变，我们可能会迎来更多破纪录的气温，部分地区会出现夏季酷暑难耐、冬季温暖和煦的情况。

8
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:15,840
This means for some, snowy winters could become a thing of the past.
这意味着对一些地方来说，飘雪的冬天可能会成为历史。

9
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:26,820
In the UK, a series of projections, based on accelerating global emissions, found that the average coldest day would not drop below freezing point.
在英国，一系列基于全球排放加速增长的预测显示，当地最冷日子的平均气温将不会跌破冰点。

10
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:45,300
Dr Lizzie Kendon, a senior Met Office scientist, told the BBC: “It could mean the end of sledging, snowmen and snowball fights… the overarching picture is warmer, wetter winters; hotter, drier summers.”
英国气象局资深科学家莉齐·肯顿博士在接受BBC采访时表示：“这可能意味着滑雪橇、堆雪人、打雪仗这些活动将成为历史……总体趋势就是冬季变得更暖更湿，夏季变得更热更干。”

11
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:48,960
She’s described this as ‘a wake-up call’.
她将这种情况称为一次“警钟”。

12
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:56,230
Reducing greenhouse gas emissions is the obvious way to slow the rate of change in our climate.
减少温室气体排放是减缓气候变化速度的有效途径。

13
00:01:56,230 --> 00:02:05,150
Some nations are promising to do this, but already we’re experiencing less snowfall and fewer frosty mornings.
一些国家已承诺会采取相关措施，但我们已经在经历降雪量减少、霜冻清晨变少的状况。

14
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:09,110
And on a bigger scale, glaciers are melting.
从更大范围来看，冰川也在不断消融。

15
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:21,640
According to modelling by Aberystwyth University in the UK, up to 92% of glaciers in the Alps could be lost by the end of the century due to climate change.
英国阿伯里斯特威斯大学的模型研究显示，到本世纪末，气候变化可能会导致阿尔卑斯山高达92%的冰川消失。

16
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:31,180
So, if you’re lucky enough to be looking out on a winter wonderland, get outside and make the most of it before it melts.
所以，如果你有幸能看到银装素裹的冬日美景，一定要出门去，在它消融前好好享受这份景致。
